# Security Audit & Vulnerability Testing Sub-Skill

When invoked standalone or by `security-orchestrator`, systematically audit against OWASP Top 10 risk vectors:

## 1. Injection Vulnerabilities (SQLi, Command Injection, XSS)
- Check for unescaped user inputs in raw SQL queries, shell commands (`exec`, `eval`), and HTML rendering.
- Verify ORM parameterized queries or sanitized template strings are used.

## 2. Broken Authentication & Session Management
- Ensure passwords are hashed with strong algorithms (Argon2, bcrypt, scrypt).
- Verify JWT tokens have strict signature checks, expiration (`exp`), and secure storage flags (`HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Strict`, `Secure`).

## 3. Sensitive Data Exposure & Crypto Audit
- Ensure proper encryption for data at rest and in transit (TLS 1.3, AES-256-GCM).
- Flag weak algorithms (MD5, SHA1, ECB mode encryption).

## 4. Broken Access Control (IDOR & Privilege Escalation)
- Verify endpoint authorization middleware on every private route.
- Test for Insecure Direct Object References (IDOR) on entity IDs (e.g. `/api/users/:id`).

## 5. Security Misconfigurations
- Check CORS configurations for overly permissive wildcards (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` with credentials).
- Ensure debug modes are disabled for production builds.

## Output Requirements
Return identified risks categorized with Severity levels: **[CRITICAL]**, **[HIGH]**, **[MEDIUM]**, **[LOW]**, specifying file path, line numbers, Proof of Concept, and remediation code.
